Radio Bart

"Radio Bart" adalah episode ketiga belas dari musim ketiga The Simpsons. Episode tersebut awalnya disiarkan dalam saluran Fox di Amerika Serikat pada 9 Januari 1992.
<h2>Referensi</h2>
Referensi.
Now I made a plot for Band Together (the Jack's Super Swell Sing-Along remake.) Here's the plot.
Plot:
The series focuses on newcomer Keys Sharps 'N' Flats , who wants to play a live concert on her piano. While practicing overnight and imagining her dream come true, Jewel Sparkles listens to her from a distance while going to sleep and was struck by the lyrics of the song as she heard the phrase "Sparkle and shine like the star you are" and thought that focused on her because "Sparkles" is her last name, so she goes to his house and proposes to be famous under his managerial tutelage. Dot meanwhile discovers a constellation that only appears with music.
Meanwhile, Spot begins to be inspired by Keys' music after running out of ideas for a new piece of art. In the morning, Jewel suggests to Keys that they look for band members and introduces Ace's garage as her practice spot. Dot meanwhile tells Bea about her discovery of a galaxy that only appears when music is played.
A day later, Ace, Dot, Bea, and Spot apply as band candidates, but fail to qualify to be inducted into the band. Later while Forest was looking for maple syrup, he meets Sticks who had just moved to Lalaloopsyland and was practicing alone in the middle of the forest. After seeing her file while she was leaving, Forest suggests to Sticks to compete as a drummer for the band, to which she accepts. In a subsequent scene change, Strings and her cat Tabby are introduced who are late for the audition. After the three girls meet, they introduce themselves and play together but Sticks does a drum solo that throws the rest of the girls off balance.
Jewel names the newly formed band " The Buttonnettes " and suggests they go on tour throughout Lalaloopsy Land , but Keys is initially concerned due to her stage fright and to resolve this issue, suggests the girls keep practicing. At night, Jewel goes to Spot to ask for a poster for the band, who is inspired by the music of the Buttonnettes. While Bea and Dot coordinate to see Dot's new musical constellation by bus because the latter can't see the stars because of the lights. Brody and Jewel are about to introduce the next guest, but Jewel has forgotten her line. The Schwartzman Quartet enter, singing "Barbershop Song."
In the morning, Sticks is late and Jewel shows them the official poster for the band. Later, Sticks doesn't get in sync with the girls and they have a little argument where the former retreats into the woods after being criticized. Spot meanwhile, loses inspiration in making a harp out of a chair when he stops listening to the band's music.
Sticks meets Forest and tells her that even though she's good at doing things alone, sometimes you have to work as a team to be a part of something bigger. Said advice arose after Sticks realized that her music without the girls is not the same. Suddenly, the girls arrive and apologize by composing a passing song proving that they are better together and continue to play it as a practice song. Spot in passing listens to the song again and is inspired to finish his extravagant creation.
In the morning, Dot and Bea arrive by bus with a telescope as a way of lending the vehicle to the girls and at the same time convincing them to accompany them on the tour, while Ace and Spot also arrive on the scene as the band's mechanic and as a fan in search of inspiration respectively. Later, the girls prepare the bus by painting it and head out on the tour, but Keys remains undecided due to her stage fright.
At night, the girls arrive but Keys abruptly leaves the stage in the middle of the concert and all the other leads and supporting girls follow them to find out what happened as their interesting side events disappeared with Keys leaving. The latter comments that she has stage fright, but Jewel and the girls encourage her to sing again by telling her that they are a band (Buttonnetes), that she was sewn for this job and that events that the other girls like (The Girls) derive from her music. Dot's stars and Spot's new inspiration). Keys, already animated again, goes on a tour to the next destination: a stage in a clearing in Lalaloopsy Land, but it takes them a whole day to get there because the bus breaks down.
Upon arriving there, the Buttonnettes do well with their performance and Jewel wears her ball gown calling out Peanut, Crumbs, and Peanut respectively. Meanwhile Bea, Dot, Ace and Spot concentrate on their activities derived from the music of the Buttonnettes. Having overcome their stage fright, it is assumed that the Buttonnetes did well in their next destinations considering the end of Keys' own conflict.
