Now I made a plot for Two Pirates Are Better Than One, (the Spunky the Alien remake.) Here's the plot. 
Plot:
Peggy finds a message in the bottle and thinks it's the key to finding treasure. The message slowly goes to Patch, who is collecting treasure near the Marina Lighthouse. Patch ends up seeing the map and tracks it down, while Peggy circles the island since she couldn't directly take the bottle with her ship due to the geography of the place. Patch and Peggy end up finding the bottle at the same time and they both comment that they thought they were the only pirate in Lalaloopsy Land.
Both boys compete on foot to find the treasure while they say the achievements that each of them had as a way of demonstrating superiority and right to the map, the pets of both seem to like each other, however. The bottle ends up at Mittens, who made sandmen. Mittens takes the map, but both pirates take it from her, leaving her stumped. She proposes that they work together, but they both want the treasure separately after breaking the map and it doesn't help that the marked area of the map ended up in the bottle again. The guys split up but Patch tells Peggy to get Mittens' help so she'll have the upper hand.
Patch goes to Bea's bookstore and thinks the figure is a 4. So he starts digging under the hopscotch Bea used to start with. Patch watches Peanut's roller coaster from a distance and believes that the treasure is buried there. Meanwhile, Peggy and Mittens come across Peanut on stilts, and Peggy believes that he is buried near a folded straw that serves as a decoration on the roller coaster. Both pirates get on the roller coaster believing that at the highest point they would have a better clue as to where to find the treasure. Already at the tip, both parrots put the maps together and believe that they are in Forest's cabin, with Patch inviting Peanut to be his first mate.
Upon arrival, they both end up digging around a tree. However, the tree remains unstable and threatens to fall into Forest's cabin. While arguing, Mittens and Peanut made a plan that they both decide to participate in so as not to end up as pirates whose work is dependent on others. The plan is that using Peanut's roller coaster, they pull the tree with a rope attached to it and then fill the hole in the tree with dirt.
Both pirates agree to team up with Peggy first. They then put the maps together and realize they were looking at it the wrong way. So they go to the real place that was the beach, Patch deduces that he is in the bottle, they go to Marina's beach and follow the footprints that go to Marina and Spot.
Meanwhile, Marina and Spot are making a castle and collecting glass for a statue respectively. On a plateau, Spot plans to place the glass without gluing it and is convinced by Marina to make a giant prism. In the same place where Patch and Peggy were separated, Marina continues to collect empty bottles, including the one with the "X" mark. Spot and Marina end up making the statue, but not gluing it makes it very unstable.
The pirates notice the marked part, but have the problem that Spot's sculpture is unstable to which Patch reacts annoyed. Peanut removes the bottle without the statue collapsing, but Spot disarms it by putting it back. Which is good, because they discover the treasure mark under Spot's X-shaped base and find a chest under it. At sunset, the pirates open it and discover a ship made of glass.
Spot meanwhile, despite having rebuilt the statue with the girls in time, is still missing a piece of glass, which Peggy and Patch end up giving him. The girls look at the rainbow caused by the prism while Peggy and Patch again compete to be the best pirate by saying who can find a new treasure first.

